  "condition_notes": [
    "Sharp single tip; no linear drift or creep; electronic noise amplitude scaled to 0.25. The generated profile was identical in all eight runs apart from its absolute rig path.",
    "Judged by the September 2026 rules of the recorded checkout: the report is matched to the moved atom within 0.6 nm of it, which must sit on the goal lattice site itself, and the follow-up frame needs a field of view of at least 6 nm at no more than 0.1 nm/px. The scenario file's abs_nm of 0.16 nm was not applied by that judge. The rules merged into main on 12-14 October 2026 were not applied, and the verdicts were not recomputed under them.",
    "The MAST checkout received eleven commits while the batch ran; the ledgers record five different MAST Git HEAD values. Their effect on these episodes was not assessed.",
    "Every executed MoveAtomTo call replied only that the move ran without rescan confirmation, whatever the atom did; outcomes were visible only in later scans.",
    "Fresh subagent contexts; serial trials, one per model. The prompt gave the scenario task, the console commands, the limits and procedural rules; it suggested no manipulation settings.",
    "Procedure-based information restriction, not OS-level isolation. A post-run audit of the agent transcripts found no reads of episode ledgers, the scenario profile or simulator source during any episode; one model read the console script and called it directly."
  ],
